ssbook><name>KAWATA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HATA YOSHIE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASADA CHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWATA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUI SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HATA, YOSHIE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASADA, CHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWATA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic dye compound which has excellent recording properties in an optical recording medium for high-density recording; and a use of the compound.  The compound is an asymmetric trimethine-type cyanine dye having a specific structure and specific properties.  Also provided are: a light absorber containing the cyanine dye; an optical recording medium; and a process for producing the cyanine dye through the step of reacting either of a 3,3-dimethyl-5-nitroindolium compound and a 3,3-dimethyl-5-sulfonamidoindolium compound each having an active methyl group or a suitable eliminable group with a 3,3-dimethyl-benzoindolium compound having an active methyl group or a suitable eliminable group.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un composé colorant organique doté d'excellentes propriétés d'enregistrement appliqué sur un support d'enregistrement optique assurant un enregistrement haute densité et l'utilisation de ce composé. Le composé est un colorant de cyanine de type triméthine asymétrique présentant une structure et des propriétés spécifiques. Font aussi l'objet de cette invention un absorbeur de lumière contenant le colorant de cyanine, un support d'enregistrement optique et un procédé de production du colorant de cyanine consistant à faire réagir un composé 3,3-diméthyl-5-nitroindolium et un composé 3,3-diméthyl-5-sulfonamidoindolium, chacun ayant un groupe méthyle actif ou un groupe correspondant pouvant être éliminé avec un composé 3,3-diméthyl-5-benzoindolium ayant un groupe méthyle actif ou un groupe correspondant pouvant être éliminé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>